  "body": "## What changed\nRequire both rim-vertex neighbours to stand beyond CROSSING_TOUCH on opposite sides of the trace.\nUse a length-scaled band for straight segments and polyline footprints.\nUse a radial distance band for XY arcs.\nKeep sub-band wall wobble under the wall check.\n\n## Cause\nExact sign tests treated neighbours almost on the trace as a crossing.\nThat classification excused the move from the wall check.\n\n## Tests\nAll three pins failed on unchanged production code and pass with the fix.\n- rim_vertex_segment_neighbours_need_distance_band covers straight and polyline traces at two lengths and preserves true crossings.\n- rim_vertex_arc_neighbours_need_distance_band covers the arc branch and preserves true crossings.\n- rim_vertex_wall_wobble_still_answers_to_walls covers a lattice wall with sub-band perpendicular wobble.\n\nRestoring the old segment guard makes the segment and wall pins fail.\nRestoring the fix makes all three pins pass.\nRestoring the old arc guard makes the arc pin fail.\nRestoring the fix makes all three pins pass.\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passes.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings` passes.\n\n## Goldens moved\nNone.\n`git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\nThe full release gate and physical machine execution were not run.\n\n## Overlaps\nNo open PR touched either changed source file at the overlap check.\n\nEffort: high.\nChangelog: Keep near-trace wall wobble under verification by requiring a distance band for rim-vertex crossings.\nFixes #1669\n",
